  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user, I want the app's tables to keep the legacy row height and grey chevrons, so that rows are easy to tap and every table looks the same.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 05, 14 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Observed (2026-11-11)\n- **Plus**: legacy rows are taller; SwiftHFR rows are standard height. Chevrons: legacy neutral grey, SwiftHFR pale accent colour. \"Supprimer mon compte\": legacy has no chevron (an action, not a navigation); SwiftHFR adds one and a darker red.\n- **Catégories** (@ `9e93c3eb`, after #427): no chevron on the rows; legacy has a discreet grey one.\n- **Topic-list segmented control** (Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus): legacy fills the selected segment with the accent colour, SwiftHFR uses the native style. **Operator undecided**: to settle here.\n\n### Scope\n- One shared row style for these tables: legacy height, grey chevron, none on action rows, system red for destructive rows.\n- Apply to Plus, Catégories, Réglages and the other tables that use the legacy table look.\n\nRelated: #572 (umbrella: one row, separator and state-tint definition), #799 (margins and density), #427.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
